Phase 4 Task 1 — always-on prayer-fired scheduler event.

fire_prayer (src-tauri/src/scheduler/mod.rs) now builds the {prayer, time}
payload once and:
1. Emits "prayer-fired" unconditionally — independent of the
   notification_enabled / adhan_enabled toggles. Drives the new in-app
   prayer-time prompt (PrayerPrompt) which offers the one-tap "Prayed"
   action on any screen. OS notifications cannot carry action buttons on
   desktop (tauri-plugin-notification 2.3.3 desktop path is plain
   notify_rust — no action API, no click events; see spec amendment
   2026-08-20), so the prompt is the desktop one-tap path.
2. Emits "prayer-time" only when adhan_enabled (unchanged AdhanPlayer
   behavior).

Test-exempt per project rule: fire_prayer is event glue requiring a live
AppHandle (no logic-bearing code changed). cargo test 119 unit + 6
integration pass; no regression.
